1. What is IAM?

IAM = Identity and Access Management
IAM answers two fundamental questions:

Who are you?

What are you allowed to do?
For example:

DevOps Engineer
      ↓
     IAM
      ↓
 ┌────┼────────────┐
 ↓    ↓            ↓
 EC2  S3          RDS
 ✓    ✓            ✗

The DevOps engineer might be allowed to work with EC2 and S3 but not modify the production database.


2. Real-World Analogy 🏢

Imagine an office.

There are:

Employees
Managers
Security guards
IT administrators
Visitors

Everyone doesn't get access to every room.

For example:

Employee
   ↓
Office ✓
Server Room ✗
CEO Room ✗

IAM works similarly.

AWS Account
    ↓
   IAM
    ↓
Who can access what?
